    <p>Q1. The UC8 lookup table has 65536 entries. Why 65536 specifically?</p>
    <ul class="options">
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="65536 = 2^16, but that's not the connection here. The 2^16 entries come from 256 possible I values × 256 possible Q values, not from the uint16_t output range.">Because uint16_t can hold values 0–65535</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="Not quite — there are 256 I values AND 256 Q values. The table indexes the pair (I, Q) together.">Because each byte has 256 possible values</li>
      <li data-correct="true" data-why="Correct. 256 possible values for I × 256 possible values for Q = 65536 total unique (I, Q) pairs. Every possible combination of raw dongle bytes has one precomputed entry.">256 I values × 256 Q values = every possible input pair</li>
      <li data-correct="false" data-why="The sample rate is 2.4 MHz but the table size comes from the input value range, not the sample rate.">Because the RTL-SDR sample rate is 2.4 MHz</li>
    </ul>
